{"hits": {"hits": [{"links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/123995?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/123995?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/123995?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/123995?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/123995?format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/123995?format=cv", "citations": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A123995"}, "updated": "2025-10-30T13:06:45.687634+00:00", "metadata": {"authors": [{"full_name": "Kuraev, E.A."}, {"full_name": "Lipatov, L.N."}, {"full_name": "Fadin, Victor S."}], "publication_info": [{"journal_volume": "45", "page_end": "204", "year": 1977, "journal_record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1214386"}, "page_start": "199", "journal_title": "Sov.Phys.JETP"}, {"journal_volume": "72", "artid": "377", "page_end": "389", "year": 1977, "journal_record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1214339"}, "page_start": "377", "journal_issue": "2", "journal_title": "Zh.Eksp.Teor.Fiz."}], "texkeys": ["Kuraev:1977fs"], "imprints": [{"date": "1977"}, {"date": "1977-02"}], "abstracts": [{"value": "An integral equation is derived for the $t$-channel partial wave amplitudes in the investigation of the multi-Regge form of the $2\\to 2+n$ amplitude. For a $t$-channel state with isospin $T=1$ the solution of this equation is a Regge pole. The analytic properties os the isospin $T=0$, $2$ partial wave amplitudes are investigated near the threshold for the production of two or three particles. It is shown that in the $j$-plane there are moving poles and cuts. For the $T=0$ vacuum channel it was found that the partial wave amplitude has a fixed square-root type branch point to the right of $j=1$."}], "control_number": 123995, "titles": [{"title": "The Pomeranchuk singularity in nonabelian gauge theories"}, {"title"